MediaPipe models and reference geometry
--------------------------------------
Copyright 2019-2025 The MediaPipe Authors / Google LLC
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE-APACHE).
Upstream: https://github.com/google-ai-edge/mediapipe

This distribution contains ONNX conversions of Google's face_detector.tflite
(BlazeFace short-range) and face_landmarks_detector.tflite (Face Landmarker v2,
478 points), from the version 1 float16 face_landmarker.task bundle:
https://storage.googleapis.com/mediapipe-models/face_landmarker/face_landmarker/float16/1/face_landmarker.task

The conversions were produced with tf2onnx 1.17.0, opset 17. Format and tensor
representation were changed; no retraining was performed. Exact source and
converted SHA-256s, conversion instructions, and model scope are in models/.

The landmark decoder follows the MediaPipe v0.10.32 face detector and landmark
graphs (Copyright 2023-2025 The MediaPipe Authors). The seven canonical-face
vertices in crates/lucas-gaze/src/features.rs are adapted from MediaPipe's
canonical_face_model.obj (Copyright 2020 The MediaPipe Authors).

The test/optional headless-diagnostic portrait.jpg is MediaPipe's Apache-2.0 test asset from
https://storage.googleapis.com/mediapipe-assets/portrait.jpg . It is not a user
webcam recording. Its provenance and SHA-256 are in the fixture README.

These third-party materials remain Apache-2.0 and are not relicensed under
LUCAS's MIT option. No upstream NOTICE file is present in the model archive.

Optional UniGaze downloads (not included in this distribution)
-------------------------------------------------------------
The explicit setup script downloads UniGaze-H joint weights and official code
from https://github.com/ut-vision/UniGaze at revision
9c240fbe33f3d6146970a77b7c8fa06a7e60019e. Authors: Jiawei Qin, Xucong Zhang,
Yusuke Sugano. UniGaze: Towards Universal Gaze Estimation via Large-scale
Pre-Training, WACV 2026. The source archive retains its MG-NC-RAI-2.0 license.
The imported normalization module retains CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 and cites:
Xucong Zhang, Yusuke Sugano, Andreas Bulling, Revisiting Data Normalization for
Appearance-Based Gaze Estimation, ETRA 2018.
The SFD/FAN frontend is provided by https://github.com/1adrianb/face-alignment.
Downloaded source, weights, CUDA/PyTorch dependencies and their upstream licenses
are not relicensed under LUCAS's MIT option. See models/unigaze/README.md and its
asset/dependency locks for provenance and the local adapter's changes.
